exg-c — unaffiliated 8-channel EXG host (C)

Build:  make
Run:    ./np-exg
        ./np-exg --cli --port /dev/ttyUSB1 --seconds 8

Requires libSDL2, dialout (or the launcher re-execs via sg).
Settings persist in ~/.config/exg-c.conf

Keys: c connect  d disconnect  r record  space pause  1-8 toggle  q quit
Click View buttons for window, scale, 50/60 Hz notch, high-pass, grid.
Learn: click the name box, type a label, hold the pose, Save. MATCH scores
the live window against every saved sample. Same name overwrites.
Learn always runs hp 2 Hz, a 40 Hz low-pass, and the mains notch (50 if
view notch is off) so rail hiss and 50/60 Hz do not dominate the score.
Samples persist in ~/.config/exg-c.learn
Firmware on the board is 125 SPS; the status line shows measured rate.

USB frames keep coming when the analog switches are off — those switches
only route the front-end, they do not stop acquire_data(). Open inputs
sit at the ADS1299 rail (~±0.13 V) and are labeled open/rail, not EEG.
Lead-off bits (frame bytes 18–19) are shown when the firmware sets them.
